### Security
Two profiles, selected by the `petclinic.security.enable` property:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/BasicAuthenticationConfig.java` — active when `petclinic.security.enable=true`. Enables `@EnableMethodSecurity(prePostEnabled=true)` (so the controller's `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` is enforced → requires role `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`), CSRF disabled, HTTP Basic, all requests authenticated, JDBC-backed users/roles.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/DisableSecurityConfig.java` — active when `=false`. CSRF disabled, `anyRequest().permitAll()`, `frameOptions sameOrigin`. With method security not enabled here, the `@PreAuthorize` is effectively not enforced.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/Roles.java` (`@Component` named `roles`): `OWNER_ADMIN = "ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN"`, referenced via SpEL `@roles.OWNER_ADMIN`.

Defaults: `src/main/resources/application.properties:49` sets `petclinic.security.enable=false` (security off in the normal run); the test config `src/test/resources/application.properties` sets it to `true` and context-path `/petclinic/`.

### Filters / interceptors
No custom servlet `Filter`, `OncePerRequestFilter`, `HandlerInterceptor`, `WebMvcConfigurer`, or `FilterRegistrationBean` exist in the project — the only request-chain filters are Spring Security's own (from the config above). `@CrossOrigin` on the controller adds CORS handling.

